        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अभ्यर्थयते",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अभ्यर्थयते — abhyarthayate — \"requests; asks for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि भवान् अभ्यर्थयते, तर्हि सः साहाय्यं करिष्यति। yadi bhavān abhyarthayate, tarhi saḥ sāhāyyaṃ kariṣyati. If you ask him, he will help."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः साहाय्यम् अभ्यर्थितवान्, saḥ sāhāyyam abhyarthitavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अभ्यर्थयते (abhyarthayate) is built on abhi, \"towards\", and the verb arthaya, \"to ask, to wish\"; MW gives abhy-√arth \"to request, to ask for\" and abhy-arthita \"asked, invited\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
